 a hurdle both men have  to maneuver around the trot is also a  symbol of dumbledore and grindelwald's  devotion toward each other something  that still exists despite being on  opposite sides of the upcoming war until  this movie dumbledore has been resistant  to take a stand against grindelwald not  just because he can't but because he  doesn't want to when dumbledore and  grindelwald face off a heart appears in  the blood trough and the beating of two  hearts plays out over the sounds of  battle both wizards hesitate but the  damage is done and the vial breaks a  clear symbol of dumbledore's heart  breaking in the process when asked how  dumbledore could move against  grindelwald when the troth was still  intact the professor says he sought to  kill i sought to protect our spells met  let's call it fate but fate or not  dumbledore looks pretty miserable at the  prospect of having to defeat the man he  loved with or without you i'll burn down  their world  the secrets of dumbledore may be the  first time dumbledore and grindelwald  raise their wands against each other but  it won't be the last in one of the most  epic duels we've seen in the fantastic  beasts series thus far the one-time  partners accept their fate as enemies  albeit a little half-heartedly they can  only duel after grindelwald fires a  killing curse at vicenzia santos after  she wins the election or credence  inventions for failing him of course  dumbledore can't sit around and watch  his ex-lover kill someone so he takes a  stand locking the two in battle it's  important to note that neither wizard  casts a killing curse both men cast  reddish spells and there's no avada  cadaver green in sight not even after  the blood trot breaks so it seems as  though grindelwald's call for  dumbledore's death might have been a bit  premature and it's implied that gellert  doesn't want dumbledore dead sure he may  have enlisted credence to kill his uncle  still perhaps he knew all along that the  obscurial wa